<blockquote>
<p>Who this is for: people who treat "the demo worked once" as a conclusion; people whose CI is green and who keep getting hit by the first prompt a user types; people about to add evaluation to an agent and unsure where to start.</p>
<p><strong>TL;DR:</strong> one passing run is a sample, not a result. An agent's output is a joint distribution over model, tools and environment, and a single run samples one point. Evaluation needs a denominator, a definition of success, and assertions about the process. NanoHermes has ninety unit tests and five end-to-end cases, and its mock reads each request and throws it away. Make the tool list return an empty array and all five end-to-end cases still pass.</p>
<p>Reading time around 36 minutes. Level: advanced.</p>
</blockquote>

